		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>We present MeSSI, a multi-module system applied to SemEval 2025&apos;s task 3: MuSHROOM. Our system tags questions in order to obtain semantic relevant terms that are used as information retrieval characteristics. Said characteristics serve as extraction terms for Wikipedia pages that are in turn processed to generate gold standard texts used in a hallucination evaluation system. A part-of-speech-tag based entity comparison was implemented to contrast the test dataset sentences with the corresponding generated gold standards, which in turn was the main criterion to tag hallucinations, partitioned in soft labels and hard labels. This method was tested in Spanish and English, finishing 18th and 19th respectively on the IoU based ranking.</p>
			</abstract>
